  "summary_en": "Canada's first AI strategy for the federal public service (2025-2027) sets four priorities: central AI capacity, policy and governance, talent and training, and engagement and transparency. It plans governance and risk frameworks, an AI ethics review board, a public AI register, and training. It is about government administrative AI, not robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establish an AI Centre of Expertise to support departments",
   "Create common AI governance and risk management frameworks scaled to risk, plus an AI ethics review board",
   "Build a public register of federal AI systems and set disclosure and recourse requirements",
   "Develop AI training and talent plans for public servants",
   "Require departments to identify AI opportunities and align policy; renew strategy in 2027"
